# AI Hub — privileged volume provisioning (AIHUB-SPEC-001, PRIV-02/PRIV-03).
#
# Install to /etc/sudoers.d/aihub-volume, owned root:root, mode 0440.
# Validate with `visudo -c -f` BEFORE installing — a malformed sudoers file can
# lock every user out of sudo.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why this grant is exactly one path with no arguments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The obvious formulation would enumerate the underlying commands, e.g.
#
#     nemr ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/losetup --find --show /home/nemr/.local/share/aihub/volumes/*.img
#
# That does not do what it appears to do. Per sudoers(5):
#
#     "Note that a forward slash ('/') will not be matched by wildcards used
#      in the file name portion of the command. [...] When matching the command
#      line arguments, however, a slash does get matched by wildcards since
#      command line arguments may contain arbitrary strings and not just path
#      names."
#
# So `volumes/*.img` also matches `volumes/../../../../etc/anything.img`, and
# the equivalent rule for `mount` would permit mounting over any host path.
# A rule of that shape looks narrow and is, in effect, passwordless root.
#
# A path constraint therefore cannot be expressed in sudoers at all. It has to
# live in code the granted user cannot modify — which is the root-owned helper
# this rule points at. The helper takes a volume NAME and a SIZE PRESET, never
# a path, device, or uid, and constructs and validates everything internally.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The grant
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# No wildcards anywhere. No arguments specified, which means the helper may be
# run with any arguments — that is intentional and safe, because the helper
# validates its own input and every argument space it accepts is closed
# (subcommand from a fixed set, name matched against ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$,
# size from a fixed list of three presets).
#
# Replace `nemr` with the account that runs the engine.

nemr ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/aihub-volume

# Notes:
#
# - /usr/local/libexec/aihub-volume must be owned root:root, mode 0755. If the
#   invoking user can write to the helper, this grant becomes unrestricted
#   root. Verify with: stat -c '%U:%G %a' /usr/local/libexec/aihub-volume
#
# - The helper refuses to run unless SUDO_UID/SUDO_GID are set, so it does
#   nothing useful if executed directly as root.
#
# - `sudo -n` is used by the engine so a missing or revoked rule fails
#   immediately with a clear error instead of blocking on a password prompt.
